From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:32:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 55/58] fix(media): media events carry what Wallpaper Engine's
 do, times in seconds

MPRIS gives a track's length and position in microseconds, and scripts
were handed them as they came; MediaTimelineEvent is in seconds, so a
progress bar crawled and a "3:35" duration read as a number of minutes
in the millions. They are seconds now.

MediaPropertiesEvent lacked albumArtist, subTitle, genres and
contentType, and MediaThumbnailEvent lacked textColor. A script that
falls back to the album artist when a track names no artist, and one
that colors a progress bar with the text color, both threw on the first
event. albumArtist and genres come from the player's metadata (genres
separated by ", "); MPRIS names no subtitle or content type, so those
are "". textColor is white, the only color of the fixed palette that
contrasts with its primary color.

DBusMediaSource::readMetadata reads a Metadata dictionary into a
MediaInfo and says what changed, so tests build one without a bus. An
artist list that comes empty now clears the last track's artist.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
